nio: start the USB gadget by default (enabled 1 -> 2)

Run 659 finally compiled the ECM/live-log code, but sweet's port defaults
`enabled = 1` (probe only) and only starts the gadget at niousb=2.  nio's
boot args do not pass niousb=2, so no USB device ever appears.  Default to
2 so the gadget and its live-log UDP stream start on every boot, matching
the earlier 526-line driver.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c b/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
--- a/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/nio_usb.c
@@ -73,4 +73,4 @@ nio_usb_gadget_probe(void)
 {
-	int enabled = 1;
+	int enabled = 2;
 	uint32_t gdscr, cbcr[sizeof(usb_cbcr) / sizeof(usb_cbcr[0])];
 	bool clocks_on = true;
